Portions of the structuring and region-recovery code are ported from angr
(https://github.com/angr/angr), released under the BSD 2-Clause License;
ported algorithms are tagged with their source decompiler in
decompiler/crates/kuna-decomp/phases.toml and docs/spec/.

The JVM engine (decompiler/nonnative/kuna-jvm) is a Rust port of Vineflower
1.12.0 (https://github.com/Vineflower/vineflower), released under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. Vineflower is a fork of JetBrains' Fernflower,
MinecraftForge's ForgeFlower and FabricMC's fork of Fernflower, and a
continuation of Quiltflower; its ported source files carry these notices:

    Copyright 2000-2022 JetBrains s.r.o.
    Copyright 2000-2022 JetBrains s.r.o. and ForgeFlower contributors
    Copyright 2019 FabricMC project
    Use of this source code is governed by the Apache 2.0 license.

with the remaining portions copyright the Vineflower contributors. The JVM
regression corpus (tests/jvm/) is derived from Vineflower's test data
(copyright JetBrains s.r.o. and the Vineflower contributors, Apache License,
Version 2.0): class files compiled or assembled from its testData sources, the
class files it ships there, and the Java text the released vineflower-1.12.0.jar
prints for them; its provenance is recorded in tests/jvm/README.md.

